\name{cellucid_history_step_revert}
\alias{cellucid_history_step_revert}
\title{Revert a step}
\usage{
cellucid_history_step_revert(viewer, step)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{step}{A step of the tracker in use, by its id (history_get lists the steps). Text. Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome (what it did, as names, counts and ids), or \code{NULL} when it had nothing to report; \code{request$step} is the history step it made.
}
\description{
Add a step that puts back exactly what a step changed, when no later step on the path changed the same parts (else use Branch without a step).
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.step.revert} (History). It changes the viewer's state: one step of the viewer's history, labeled as R's, undone like any other. The state it can change: \code{cells}, \code{mapping}, \code{expression}, \code{field-overlays}, \code{gene-sets}, \code{views}, \code{active-field}, \code{filters}, \code{colors}, \code{visibility}, \code{highlights}, \code{camera}, \code{camera-path}, \code{settings}, \code{analysis}, \code{layout}.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_step_revert(viewer, step = "s3")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
